<title>MOLDOVA: Moldovan inflation slowed to 1.6 pct in Oct.</title>
<headline>Moldovan inflation slowed to 1.6 pct in Oct.</headline>
<dateline>CHISINAU 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Moldovan consumer prices rose 1.6 percent in October, a slightly slower pace of inflation than September's 1.5 percent, an official from the State Statistics Department told Reuters on Thursday.</p>
<p>    MOLDOVAN CONSUMER PRICES     Oct '96   Sept '96    Oct '95</p>
<p>    Monthly pct change		  +1.6	 +1.5	 +2.7</p>
<p>    Year-on-year pct change	    +23	  +24	  +21</p>
<p>Consumer prices in the first 10 months of 1996 grew by 12.5 percent. The National Bank expects annual inflation to slow this year to 15-17 percent from 23.8 percent in 1995.</p>
<p>--Dmitry Solovyov, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
